1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,160
Luke 11

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:09,440
Now Jesus was praying in a certain place, and when he finished, one of his disciples said to him,

3
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:13,900
Lord, teach us to pray, as John taught his disciples.

4
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:15,780
And he said to them,

5
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:22,420
When you pray, say, Father, hallowed be your name, your kingdom come.

6
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:27,040
Give us each day our daily bread, and forgive us our sins,

7
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:30,540
for we ourselves forgive everyone who is indebted to us.

8
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:33,340
And lead us not into temptation.

9
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:35,280
And he said to them,

10
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:39,940
Which of you who has a friend will go to him at midnight and say to him,

11
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:45,180
Friend, lend me three loaves, for a friend of mine has arrived on a journey,

12
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:47,400
and I have nothing to set before him.

13
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:49,700
And he will answer from within,

14
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:54,560
Do not bother me, the door is now shut, and my children are with me in bed.

15
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:56,880
I cannot get up and give you anything.

16
00:00:57,740 --> 00:01:02,420
I tell you, though he will not get up and give him anything because he is his friend,

17
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:07,320
yet because of his impudence he will rise and give him whatever he needs.

18
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:11,900
And I tell you, ask, and it will be given to you.

19
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:13,840
Seek, and you will find.

20
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,420
Knock, and it will be opened to you.

21
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:21,280
For everyone who asks receives, and the one who seeks finds.

22
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:24,620
And to the one who knocks, it will be opened.

23
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:27,020
What father among you?

24
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:31,960
If his son asks for a fish, will instead of a fish give him a serpent?

25
00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:35,440
Or if he asks for an egg, will give him a scorpion?

26
00:01:36,140 --> 00:01:40,680
If you then, who are evil, know how to give good gifts to your children,

27
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:46,780
how much more will the heavenly Father give the Holy Spirit to those who ask him?

28
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:51,240
Now he was casting out a demon that was mute.

29
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:56,820
When the demon had gone out, the mute man spoke, and the people marveled.

30
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:58,640
But some of them said,

31
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:02,680
He cast out demons by Beelzebul, the prince of demons.

32
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:07,360
While others to test him kept seeking from him a sign from heaven.

33
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:10,460
But he, knowing their thoughts, said to them,

34
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:17,020
Every kingdom divided against itself is laid waste, and a divided household falls.

35
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:22,820
And if Satan also is divided against himself, how will his kingdom stand?

36
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:26,280
For you say that I cast out demons by Beelzebul,

37
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:27,020
and I cast out demons by Beelzebul.

38
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:32,000
And if I cast out demons by Beelzebul, by whom do your sons cast them out?

39
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:34,480
Therefore they will be your judges.

40
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:38,660
But if it is by the finger of God that I cast out demons,

41
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:41,700
then the kingdom of God has come upon you.

42
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:47,320
When a strong man, fully armed, guards his own palace, his goods are safe.

43
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:50,840
But when one stronger than he attacks him and overcomes him,

44
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:55,060
he takes away his armor in which he trusted and divides his spoil.

45
00:02:55,060 --> 00:03:01,560
Whoever is not with me is against me, and whoever does not gather with me scatters.

46
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:05,640
When the unclean spirit has gone out of a person,

47
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:11,100
it passes through waterless places seeking rest, and finding none, it says,

48
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:13,920
I will return to my house from which I came.

49
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:17,580
And when it comes, it finds the house swept and put in order.

50
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:22,060
Then it goes and brings seven other spirits more evil than itself,

51
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:24,020
and they enter and dwell there.

52
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:28,040
And the last state of that person is worse than the first.

53
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:57,900
But no sign will be given to it except the sign of Jonah.

54
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:01,560
For as Jonah became a sign to the people of Nineveh,

55
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:05,460
so will the Son of Man be to this generation.

56
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:11,180
The queen of the south will rise up at the judgment with the men of this generation

57
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:12,580
and condemn them.

58
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:16,900
For she came from the ends of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon.

59
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:20,800
And behold, something greater than Solomon is here.

60
00:04:21,620 --> 00:04:23,900
The men of Nineveh will rise up at the judgment,

61
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:26,480
with this generation, and condemn it.

62
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:29,020
For they repented at the preaching of Jonah.

63
00:04:29,420 --> 00:04:32,980
And behold, something greater than Jonah is here.

64
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:38,380
No one after lighting a lamp puts it in a cellar or under a basket,

65
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:42,060
but on a stand, so that those who enter may see the light.

66
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:45,020
Your eye is the lamp of your body.

67
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:49,200
When your eye is healthy, your whole body is full of light.

68
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:53,000
But when it is bad, your body is full of darkness.

69
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:54,000
Then it will say,

70
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,780
Therefore, be careful, lest the light in you be darkness.

71
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:03,180
If then, your whole body is full of light, having no part dark,

72
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:07,760
it will be wholly bright, as when a lamp with its rays gives you light.

73
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:13,620
While Jesus was speaking, a Pharisee asked him to dine with him,

74
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:15,820
so he went in and reclined at table.

75
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:20,740
The Pharisee was astonished to see that he did not first wash before dinner.

76
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:22,900
And the Lord said to him,

77
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:27,140
Now you Pharisees, cleanse the outside of the cup and of the dish,

78
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:30,320
but inside you are full of greed and wickedness.

79
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:31,460
You fools!

80
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:35,260
Did not he who made the outside make the inside also?

81
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:38,740
But give his alms those things that are within,

82
00:05:39,200 --> 00:05:42,060
and behold, everything is clean for you.

83
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:45,360
But woe to you Pharisees!

84
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:48,360
For you tithe mint and rue and every herb,

85
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:51,160
and neglect justice and the love of God.

86
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:52,880
These you ought to have,

87
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:55,080
without neglecting the others.

88
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,700
Woe to you Pharisees!

89
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:00,780
For you love the best seat in the synagogues,

90
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:02,720
and greetings in the marketplaces.

91
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:04,640
Woe to you!

92
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:07,120
For you are like unmarked graves,

93
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,900
and people walk over them without knowing it.

94
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:12,040
One of the lawyers answered him,

95
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:15,840
Teacher, in saying these things you insult us also.

96
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,340
And he said,

97
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:20,120
Woe to you lawyers also!

98
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:22,780
For you load people with burdens,

99
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:23,760
hard to bear,

100
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:26,200
and you yourselves do not touch the burdens

101
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:27,700
with one of your fingers.

102
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:29,660
Woe to you!

103
00:06:30,100 --> 00:06:32,080
For you build the tombs of the prophets,

104
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:33,720
whom your fathers killed.

105
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:35,440
So you are witnesses,

106
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,820
and you consent to the deeds of your fathers.

107
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:39,420
For they kill them,

108
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:41,460
and you build their tombs.

109
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:45,100
Therefore also the wisdom of God said,

110
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:47,800
I will send them prophets and apostles,

111
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:50,740
some of whom they will kill and persecute,

112
00:06:50,860 --> 00:06:52,880
so that the blood of all the prophets,

113
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:55,300
shed from the foundation of the world,

114
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:57,740
may be charged against this generation,

115
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:01,200
from the blood of Abel to the blood of Zechariah,

116
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:03,760
who perished between the altar and the sanctuary.

117
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,160
Yes, I tell you,

118
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:08,680
it will be required of this generation.

119
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,500
Woe to you lawyers!

120
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:14,340
For you have taken away the key of knowledge.

121
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:17,380
You did not enter yourselves,

122
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:20,160
and you hindered those who were entering.

123
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:22,120
As he went away from there,

124
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:25,260
the scribes and the Pharisees began to press him hard

125
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:27,720
and to provoke him to speak about many things,

126
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,280
lying in wait for him,

127
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:31,840
to catch him in something he might say.

